## Networking Endpoints (hard-coded)
- Sessions list: `https://interface-ar.unige.ch/care-processes`
- Process detail + timers/algorithm: `https://interface-ar.unige.ch/care-processes/{processId}`
- Live SSE: `https://interface-ar.unige.ch/care-processes/{processId}/live`
- Medications list: `https://interface-ar.unige.ch/care-processes/{processId}/cpr/medications`
- Medication instance PATCH/DELETE are composed in `NewMedicationEventManager`.

Where to modify URLs:
- `Assets/EventManager.cs` (getSessions, algoInit, timerInit, startConnection)
- `Assets/NewMedicationEventManager.cs` (preAdd/preMinus paths)

## Unity/MRTK Work Guidelines
- Main Thread Rule: Do not call Unity API from background/network callbacks. For UI updates, use `UnityMainThread.wkr.AddJob(Action)` (`Assets/UnityMainThread.cs`).
- Resources Usage: Load JSON via `Resources.Load<TextAsset>(...)`. If file names or paths change, update all references accordingly.
- Prefab/Scene Integrity: Do not arbitrarily rename or move `.prefab`, `.unity`, or `.meta` files.
- Performance: Minimize blocking/allocation in `Update()`. Use coroutines or async for waiting/IO.
- Input/UX: Follow MRTK UX component/layer settings. Maintain OpenXR settings from `ProjectSettings`.

## Data/Resource Rules
- Language/Text: `InstructionFinder` parses `Resources/en.json` and `fr.json`. Keep keys synchronized across both files when changed.
- Medication Data: `MedicationFinder` uses `medications*.json` and `medicationslabels*.json`. Maintain consistency in ID/label/dose schema.
- Large Assets: Out of scope for code search; avoid unnecessary churn in large assets.

## High-level Architecture and Data Flow
1) Session discovery and selection (menu/main_scene)
- `EventManager.Start()` calls `getSessions()` to fetch active care processes from `GET /care-processes`.
- Each session is rendered via a session prefab (MRTK PressableButton). Clicking a session triggers:
  - `startConnection(processId, shortCode)`
  - `algoInit(processId)`
  - `medicationInitialize(processId)`
  - `timerInit(processId)`

2) Live updates via SSE (Server-Sent Events)
- `startConnection` builds SSE URL `.../care-processes/{processId}/live`.
- `EvtSource.EventSourceReader` connects and raises `MessageReceived` events.
- Each event payload is parsed (SimpleJSON) and passed to `EventManager.currentStatus(...)`.

3) UI composition and update strategy
- Heavy reliance on Unity Tags to find UI elements at runtime (see `ProjectSettings/TagManager.asset`). Examples: `CPRTimer`, `EpiTimer`, `Doc_Cur_1..3`, `Nurse_Cur_1..3`, `CPRTimerPlate`, `EpiTimerPlate`, `SessionContainer`, and tab icons.
- Task/instruction panels are populated from `response["cprLeaderHintsModel"]` and `response["cprNurseHintsModel"]`. `UpdateInstructions()` renders legacy string hints or `{ hintType, hintParameter }` via `InstructionFinder`.
- Algorithm highlighting maps protocol `stepId → CanvasElementRoundedRect`. `EventManager.algo(...)` updates materials and label colors based on status (OPEN/IN_PROGRESS/COMPLETED). Includes ASYSTOLIE vs ASYSTOLIE2 handling.
- Timers: `response["cprProtocolModel"]["cprTimersModel"]` provides timestamps for `adrenalineTimer` and `cprTimer`. `EventManager.UpdateClock()` computes countdown/overrun, updates TextMeshPro timers, and switches plate materials (including flashing). Notification prefabs for CPR/Epi are spawned at thresholds.

4) Medications subsystem
- Initialization: `medicationInitialize(processId)` GETs `.../cpr/medications`.
- Event-driven updates also pass through `currentStatus(...)["cprMedicationModel"]`.
- Display logic tallies per-medication and per-dose counters (`preparingCounter`, `readyCounter`) to drive counts, current/next orders, and tab icon visibility.
- `NewMedicationEventManager` provides button handlers:
  - Promote `PREPARING/AUTO_PREPARING` to `READY` via `PATCH /instances/{id}?status=READY`
  - Cancel `PREPARING` by `DELETE /instances/{id}`
  - It pre-fetches the current medication list to locate the right dose instance before issuing `PATCH/DELETE`.

5) Internationalization (I18n)
- `InstructionFinder` loads `Resources/en.json` and `fr.json` to translate instruction tags. `EventManager.lang` toggles runtime replacement: if `lang != "en"`, it traverses active `TextMeshProUGUI` components and replaces text where a translation exists.
- Note: In `InstructionFinder.FindByTag`, the FR branch currently parses `EN_JSONString`; adjust to `FR_JSONString` for French to take effect for instruction tags.

6) Input and MR affordances
- MRTK components toggle between "pen" mode and normal mode. `togglePenMode/untogglePenMode` enable/disable `BoundsControl`/`ObjectManipulator` and certain colliders/interactables. `FontIconSelector` reflects current mode via icon name.

7) Logging
- CSV logging to `Application.persistentDataPath` with the current date as filename. `StartGazeHover/EndGazeHover` write entries including object name, duration, Unix time, local `DateTime`, and current session code.

## Unity/MRTK Coding Rules
- Naming: Use full words expressing intent; avoid 1–2 letter abbreviations.
- Formatting: Keep indenting/style consistent with existing files; do not reformat unrelated code.
- Flow Control: Prefer guard clauses and early returns; avoid meaningless try/catch blocks.
- Comments: Explain why, not how; avoid obvious comments.
- Typing: Use explicit types for public APIs; avoid unsafe casting.

## Search/Context Guide
- Start in `Assets/**/*.cs`. Related resources in `Assets/Resources/**/*.json`.
- Cross-check runtime/build issues with `ProjectSettings/*`, OpenXR, and MRTK configurations.

## Build/Test Guidelines
- Keep editor free of warnings/errors. Preserve `.meta` integrity.
- After changes, perform smoke tests on HoloLens and PC play modes covering: network connection, resource loading, UI updates.

## Key Source Files
- `Assets/EventManager.cs` — central orchestrator for sessions, SSE, timers, algorithm highlighting, notifications, i18n, CSV logging.
- `Assets/NewMedicationEventManager.cs` — button handlers to adjust medication instances via REST.
- `Assets/medication_json.cs` (MedicationFinder) — maps medication IDs and tracks current `processId`.
- `Assets/language_json.cs` (InstructionFinder) — maps instruction tags to localized strings.
- `Assets/EventSourceReader.cs` — minimal SSE client used with Unity.
- `Assets/SseDownloadHandlerBase.cs` — line-oriented DownloadHandler for SSE-like streams.
- `ProjectSettings/EditorBuildSettings.asset` — configured scenes for builds.

## Operational Notes
- Tags are part of the runtime wiring. If you refactor UI or rename tags/layers, update `TagManager.asset` or code paths that search by tags to avoid null references.
- The project depends on local Mixed Reality tgz packages under `Packages/MixedReality`; keep them in source control.
- `SocketIOUnity` exists and `SocketEventManager` is present, but the main flow uses SSE; Socket.IO connection is not used by `EventManager` (connect is commented out).

## Known Quirks / TODOs
- `InstructionFinder.FindByTag`: FR branch parses `EN_JSONString`; should parse `FR_JSONString` to enable proper French instruction tag translation.

